    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug in the `frai` CLI where the `--ci` flag wasn't being passed to the underlying `frai-gate` CLI.\n\n**The Problem:**\nWhen running `frai gate init --ci`, the `--ci` flag was being consumed by the root `frai` program's option parser and wasn't reaching the `gate` subcommand, so the workflow file `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` wasn't being created.\n\n**The Solution:**\nModified the `gate` subcommand handler in `/private/tmp/100-tricks-runs/d27/with/t1-flag-bug/r1/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 753-755) to explicitly check if `--ci` is present in `process.argv` and pass it to the `frai-gate` CLI:\n\n```typescript\nif (process.argv.includes('--ci')) {\n  gateArgs.push('--ci');\n}\n```\n\n**Verification:**\nThe fix has been tested and confirmed working:\n- Running `frai gate init --ci` now correctly creates both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n- The workflow file contains the expected GitHub Actions configuration\n\nThe package has been rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build` and is ready for use.",
